{"kind":"request","text":"The documentation map has the same onboarding hole from the other side. docs/README.md opens with \"Read in this order if you are new\" and lists why.md, then end-to-end.md, then concepts, then reference. It never names docs/getting-started.md. So a reader who enters through the map is sent straight to a page of runnable commands without ever being told to build the binaries or create a workroom, and end-to-end.md assumes both.\n\nThe link only runs one way today: getting-started.md points at the map, the map does not point back. The front README does link getting-started, so readers arriving there are fine; readers arriving at the documentation set itself are not.\n\nDiscovered while implementing request c3ac234a, which repairs the missing `gs init` step on the page itself. That request is about the page's own content and does not reach the map, so this is separate work rather than a widening of it. Filed before touching the map, per the discipline.","body":{"conditions":"docs/README.md names docs/getting-started.md as the first step of its ordered new-reader path, before the end-to-end walkthrough, and says in one clause what that step gives the reader — built binaries and a workroom — so the ordering reads as a reason rather than a list; the map's existing entries keep their order relative to each other; the docset anchor gate passes, confirming the link resolves; `make test` passes; reviewed by codex at an exact head before merge.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}